ColorTable08 should be bright black (dark grey), 07 should be dark white
(light gray). Magenta should be 05 and 13.
The easy way of remembering this: convert to a four bit binary  number.
IRGB (intense: aka bold aka bright)(red)(green)(blue)
0101 Magenta is made from red and blue, giving you 5 in decimal.
1101 Bright magenta is 13.

Cmd.exe uses a different color table if you are staring it with a
shortcut, so that may explain why it looks normal.

I made a little tutorial a while ago.
http://cec.wustl.edu/~naw1/console_colors.html

If I were you, I'd start with removing all ColorTable entries.


